(FMT-56 — a width and a precision written together in one format
 specifier compose: {var:8.2} asks for two decimal places, padded out to
 eight characters. LANGUAGE.md:3378-3385 (new in 0.4.10, #85). Before
 #85, {f:8.2} printed 2.5, not 2.50 — the width consumed the spec reader
 and the leftover ".2" fell to a catch-all that dropped the precision.
 On a float the digits print but the padding does not, because there is
 no float padder yet — the same limit a bare {f:8} already has.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox FMT-56.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
     255.00
   00255.00
   2.50
)
a number called n is 255.
Print "{n:8.2}".
Print "{n:08.2}".
a float called f is 2.5.
Print "{f:8.2}".
